d":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7VobeQ","user":{"login":"wandering-peak","id":162621698,"node_id":"U_kgDOCbFpAg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/162621698?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wandering-peak","html_url":"https://github.com/wandering-peak","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wandering-peak/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wandering-peak/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wandering-peak/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wandering-peak/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wandering-peak/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wandering-peak/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wandering-peak/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wandering-peak/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wandering-peak/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-27T04:25:10Z","updated_at":"2025-11-27T04:25:10Z","body":"Reproducible in 4.5.1","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3584145296/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3806098260","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112017#issuecomment-3806098260","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112017","id":3806098260,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7i3HNU","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-27T16:12:41Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T16:12:41Z","body":"Reproducible in 4.6.\n\nThe issue happens when overwriting a non coroutine (so a function without `await`) with a coroutine. When using the basetype in static typing, GDScript does not account for the possibility, that the function might actually be a coroutine in a subtype.\n\nA simple workaround is to insert an `await` into the base type implementation, so that GDScript treats the function as coroutine in all cases:\n\n```gdscript\nfunc get_bool() -> bool:\n\treturn await true\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3806098260/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3960177028","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112017#issuecomment-3960177028","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112017","id":3960177028,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7sC4GE","user":{"login":"IMP1","id":1660670,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NjA2NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1660670?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/IMP1","html_url":"https://github.com/IMP1","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IMP1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IMP1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IMP1/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IMP1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IMP1/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IMP1/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IMP1/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IMP1/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IMP1/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-25T15:41:09Z","updated_at":"2026-02-25T15:41:09Z","body":"> A simple workaround is to insert an `await` into the base type implementation, so that GDScript treats the function as coroutine in all cases:\n> \n> func get_bool() -> bool:\n> \treturn await true\n\nThis workaround isn't possible with abstract functions, which don't have a body that GDScript can identify as a coroutine.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3960177028/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3965077003","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112017#issuecomment-3965077003","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112017","id":3965077003,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7sVkYL","user":{"login":"mLampir","id":37238543,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MjM4NTQz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37238543?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mLampir","html_url":"https://github.com/mLampir","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mLampir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mLampir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mLampir/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mLampir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mLampir/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mLampir/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mLampir/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mLampir/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mLampir/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-26T08:51:57Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T08:51:57Z","body":"> > A simple workaround is to insert an `await` into the base type implementation, so that GDScript treats the function as coroutine in all cases:\n> > func get_bool() -> bool:\n> > return await true\n> \n> This workaround isn't possible with abstract functions, which don't have a body that GDScript can identify as a coroutine.\n\nFor me the workaround was casting the outcome variable of the function to it's type like\n`var result: bool = bool(res_v)`\nThis should also work for abstract functions.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3965077003/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]